# Security baseline

Financial data is **HIGHLY_SENSITIVE**.

- Every money row is scoped by `workspaceId`. Never query without it. Never leak across tenants.
- Server-side authorization on every mutation and read.
- Zod-validate all inputs.
- **Never** put balances, income, goals, account numbers, or receipts in logs, analytics, or error trackers.
- Never send more user data to an LLM than the task requires.
- Secrets only in env / secret manager. No secrets in git or client bundles.
- Audit who/what/when — no raw secrets or full financial payloads in audit blobs.
- Export and delete are Day-1 product requirements (implement with Milestone 1).
- Analytics: product events only (`Return user`, `Add Account`) — never amounts.

See skill `fintech-security-privacy` and `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`.
